# Calls that DELIBERATELY do not go through the generated client.
#
# `bun run check` runs scripts/check-api-usage.ts, which flags a raw
# fetch()/XMLHttpRequest at one of the backend's own path prefixes, a TanStack
# primitive called instead of the generated create<Op>Query/create<Op>Mutation,
# and (as a warning) a catch that throws away the error forms.ts would have
# turned into per-field messages.
#
# The generated hooks and forms.ts ARE the API surface: they carry the base
# URL, the auth header, the 401 refresh-and-retry, the typed Problem and the
# 422 → <Field> binding, and a contract change breaks the CALL SITE instead of
# the user. An escape here is a real one — an upload that needs XHR progress
# events, a third-party endpoint that happens to share a prefix, a stream the
# contract cannot describe.
#
# One entry per line: a path relative to web/, optionally narrowed to one rule,
# and ALWAYS a reason after `#` — an entry with no reason is itself an error.
#
#   src/lib/upload/xhr.ts:raw-fetch  # upload progress events; fetch has none
#   src/lib/legacy/poll.ts           # ported verbatim, rewrite tracked in #412
#
# Rules: raw-fetch, hand-rolled-hook, swallowed-error. A bare path allows all
# three in that file. An entry nothing matches is reported as a note, so this
# file stays honest as the screens change.
